        "additionalProperties": false,
        "description": "Another artifact of yours live in a frame: a page (an animated mockup in HTML, say), a dev server's or a folder's preview, or a sheet. A component canvas shows the component alone: the stories `stories` names, in that order (every story, in its file's order, when it names none), each laid out at the `width` named (else at its own `parameters.viewport`, else its content's) and drawn from its start, never scaled, and an option's media is one Preview of its poster story, the person stepping through its other states and widths in the canvas from Open full size: one wider than the room it has scrolls sideways in its well, and a card's options stand side by side only where every one fits at its width, else one under another at the card's full width. A page, a preview or a sheet is a whole screen: with no `width` it takes the card's full width at a screen's 16:10 and lays itself out to it, its card's options one under another; with a `width` it stands at that width and that screen's own height, never scaled: a phone's or a tablet's (under 768, under 1280) upright at that device's whole shape, 390×844 and 768×1024 in proportion to its width, a desk's (1280 or more) at 16:10; one wider than the room it has scrolls sideways in its well, and options stand side by side as stories do; a page taller than its frame scrolls inside it; Open full size brings it to the front of your panel."
